  "originalReleases": [
    {
      "repository": "water2004/litematica-printer",
      "id": 417572852,
      "tag_name": "v1.1.3",
      "name": "Litematica Printer 4th v1.1.3",
      "draft": false,
      "prerelease": false,
      "target_commitish": "main",
      "body": "# Litematica Printer 4th 1.1.3\r\n\r\n- Fixed ice-to-water printing above solid ground by following vanilla ice-breaking support conditions. Unsupported air below the target still prevents ice placement for water generation.\r\n- Fixed stale water-wait state blocking later ice-to-water jobs at the same position. Ice breaking now follows the regular producer-consumer cycle and respects the configured coordinate cooldown.\r\n- Preserve both upward and downward source-water bubble columns when printing ordinary water sources, instead of replacing them with ice.\r\n- Corrected the HUD waiting message so ordinary item switching is no longer described as Servux hand confirmation.\r\n- Gave filling and fluid removal their own area-selection scope options: the whole selection, below the player, or above the player. Existing settings remain compatible, and the global visible-layer restriction still applies.\r\n- Separated scan height filtering from GUI selection types while preserving live configuration changes and existing scan-range behavior.",
